(doc
  (title "YBS Framework Specification")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (section
    (heading "Overview")
    (para "**YBS (Yelich Build System)** is a meta-framework that enables AI agents to build complete software systems **autonomously** from specifications and step-by-step instructions.")
    (para "**Core Philosophy:**")
    (para "> Specifications are the single source of truth. Code is derived from specs, not the other way around.")
    (para "**Key Innovation:** Zero-interruption autonomous AI development through configuration-first design, explicit verification, and mandatory code-to-spec traceability."))
  (section
    (heading "Problems YBS Solves")
    (subsection
      (heading "1. Autonomous Execution Without Interruption")
      (item "Traditional: AI interrupts mid-build with questions")
      (item "YBS: Collects ALL decisions upfront in Step 0, enabling Steps 1-N to execute fully autonomously"))
    (subsection
      (heading "2. Code-Spec Synchronization")
      (item "Traditional: Code written first, docs written later, docs drift out of sync")
      (item "YBS: Specs are primary; code implements specs; specs stay current through change management"))
    (subsection
      (heading "3. Reproducible and Portable Builds")
      (item "Same specs + same steps = identical output every time")
      (item "Rebuild in any language/platform by pointing AI at same specs")
      (item "No \"works on my machine\" problems")))
  (section
    (heading "Core Concepts")
    (table
      (row "Concept" "Meaning" "Why It Matters")
      (row "**Spec-as-Source**" "Specifications ARE the primary artifact" "AI can regenerate code from specs at any time")
      (row "**Configuration-First**" "Step 0 collects ALL user decisions upfront" "Steps 1-N run fully autonomously")
      (row "**Traceability**" "Every line of code references its specification" "Know exactly WHY code exists")
      (row "**Verification-Driven**" "Explicit success criteria for every step" "AI knows when step is truly complete")
      (row "**Language-Agnostic**" "Works for ANY programming language or domain" "One framework rules them all")))
  (section
    (heading "Three-Layer Architecture")
    (subsection
      (heading "Layer A: Framework (Language/System Agnostic)")
      (code "ybs/framework/
├── methodology/              # How to use YBS
│   ├── overview.md
│   ├── writing-specs.md
│   ├── writing-steps.md
│   ├── executing-builds.md
│   ├── feature-addition-protocol.md
│   └── change-management.md
├── templates/                # Reusable patterns
│   ├── spec-template.md
│   ├── step-template.md
│   ├── adr-template.md
│   └── build-config-template.json
├── tools/                    # Helper scripts
│   ├── list-specs.sh
│   ├── list-steps.sh
│   ├── deps.sh
│   └── check-traceability.sh
└── docs/                     # Framework documentation
    ├── glossary.md
    ├── step-format.md
    ├── config-markers.md
    └── dependencies.md"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Layer B: System Definitions (One Per System)")
      (code "system-name/
├── README.sxp                    # System overview
├── CLAUDE.md                    # AI agent guide (system-specific)
├── specs/                       # WHAT to build (requirements)
│   ├── technical/               # Architecture, APIs
│   ├── architecture/            # Decisions, trade-offs
│   ├── business/                # Requirements, ROI
│   ├── functional/              # Features, workflows
│   ├── testing/                 # Test plans
│   ├── security/                # Security requirements (optional)
│   └── operations/              # Deployment, monitoring (optional)
├── steps/                       # HOW to build it (instructions)
│   ├── STEPS_ORDER.txt          # Execution order (CRITICAL)
│   ├── ybs-step_000000000000.md # Step 0: Build Configuration
│   ├── ybs-step_<guid>.md       # Step 1
│   ├── ybs-step_<guid>.md       # Step 2
│   └── ...                      # More steps
├── docs/                        # System-specific documentation
│   └── architecture.md
└── builds/                      # Active build workspaces
    ├── demo/
    ├── test5/
    └── production/"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Layer C: Active Builds (One Per Build Instance)")
      (code "builds/BUILDNAME/
├── BUILD_CONFIG.json            # User configuration (from Step 0)
├── BUILD_STATUS.sxp              # Progress tracking
├── SESSION.md                   # Crash recovery state (if interrupted)
├── [source code]                # Actual implementation
├── [tests]                      # Test files
├── [artifacts]                  # Build outputs
└── docs/
    └── build-history/           # Step completion records
        ├── ybs-step_000000000000-DONE.txt
        └── ybs-step_<guid>-DONE.txt")))
  (section
    (heading "Key Data Structures")
    (subsection
      (heading "BUILD_CONFIG.json")
      (para "**Purpose:** Store all configuration decisions from Step 0")
      (para "**Structure:**")
      (code "{
  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",
  \"generated\": \"2026-01-17T05:30:00Z\",
  \"system_name\": \"calculator\",
  \"values\": {
    \"system_name\": \"calculator\",
    \"language\": \"Python\",
    \"platform\": \"all\",
    \"enable_tests\": true,
    \"max_threads\": 4
  },
  \"metadata\": {
    \"total_steps\": 11,
    \"config_sources\": [\"ybs-step_000000000000\"]
  }
}")
      (para "**Key Properties:**")
      (item "Generated by Step 0, read by Steps 1-N")
      (item "If exists when Step 0 runs → skip questions, use existing config")
      (item "Machine-updatable for CI/CD automation")
      (item "Enables zero-interaction rebuilds"))
    (subsection
      (heading "BUILD_STATUS.sxp")
      (para "**Purpose:** Human-readable progress tracking")
      (para "**Contains:**")
      (item "Current step number and GUID")
      (item "Progress metrics (completed, in-progress, blocked)")
      (item "Test coverage and traceability metrics")
      (item "Issues encountered")
      (item "Next step GUID"))
    (subsection
      (heading "SESSION.md")
      (para "**Purpose:** Crash recovery - track state for resumption")
      (para "**Contains:**")
      (item "System name, build name, current step")
      (item "Timestamps (start, last update)")
      (item "Detailed progress breakdown")
      (item "Next actions")
      (item "Context notes")
      (para "**Lifecycle:**")
      (item "1. Created at session start (or loaded if exists)")
      (item "2. Updated after every significant action")
      (item "3. On completion: Moved to build-history"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Step File Format")
      (para "**File Naming:** `ybs-step_<12-hex-guid>.md` **Special:** Step 0 always uses `ybs-step_000000000000.md`")
      (para "**Structure:**")
      (code "# Step NNNNNN: [Descriptive Title]

**Version**: 0.1.0

## Overview
[What and why, 1-2 paragraphs]

## Step Objectives
1. [Specific goal 1]
2. [Specific goal 2]

## Prerequisites
- Previous step: ybs-step_[guid]
- BUILD_CONFIG.json must exist

## Configurable Values
- `{{CONFIG:key_name|type|description|default}}`
- `{{CONFIG:language|choice[Python,JavaScript]|Programming language|Python}}`

## Traceability
**Implements**: spec-file.md § X.Y (Feature Name)
**References**: D04 (Decision name)

## Instructions
### 1. [Sub-step title]
[Detailed instructions]

**Commands**:
```bash
[command examples]"))
    (subsection
      (heading "2. [Next sub-step]")
      (para "...")))
  (section
    (heading "Verification")
    (para "**This step is complete when**:")
    (item "[ ] File exists at path")
    (item "[ ] Code compiles: `npm build` succeeds")
    (item "[ ] Tests pass: `npm test` returns 0")
    (item "[ ] Verification command output matches expected")
    (para "**Verification Commands**:")
    (code "[commands to verify success]")
    (para "**Expected Output:** [what success looks like]")
    (para "**Retry Policy:**")
    (item "Maximum 3 attempts")
    (item "If 3 failures: STOP and report")
    (code "
### CONFIG Markers

**Syntax:** `{{CONFIG:key|type|description|default}}`

**Available Types:**
- `string` - Free text
- `integer`, `float` - Numbers
- `boolean` - True/false
- `choice[opt1,opt2,...]` - Single selection
- `multichoice[opt1,opt2,...]` - Multiple selections
- `color`, `url`, `email`, `path` - Specialized types

**Example:**
```markdown
- `{{CONFIG:language|choice[Swift,Python,Go]|Programming language|Swift}}`
- `{{CONFIG:max_retries|integer|Maximum retry attempts|3}}`
- `{{CONFIG:enable_logging|boolean|Enable debug logging|true}}`")
    (para "**Processing:**")
    (item "1. Step 0 scans all steps for CONFIG markers")
    (item "2. Generates questions based on markers")
    (item "3. Saves answers to BUILD_CONFIG.json")
    (item "4. Steps 1-N replace `{{CONFIG:key}}` with values from config"))
  (section
    (heading "Build Execution Protocol")
    (subsection
      (heading "State Machine")
      (code "START
  ↓
[Check for SESSION.md]
  ├→ Found: RESUME from saved state
  └→ Not found: FRESH START
  ↓
STEP 0 (Configuration Collection)
  ├→ BUILD_CONFIG.json exists: Load config, skip questions → Step 1
  └→ Doesn't exist: Ask questions, create BUILD_CONFIG.json → Step 1
  ↓
STEP 1-N (Sequential Execution)
  ↓
For each step:
  1. Read step file completely
  2. Replace {{CONFIG:key}} with values from BUILD_CONFIG.json
  3. Execute instructions step-by-step
  4. Create test files (if code implementation step)
  5. Run verification
     ├→ PASS: Mark complete, proceed to next step
     ├→ FAIL: Retry (up to 3 attempts)
     └→ 3 failures: STOP and report error
  6. Document completion (create step-DONE file)
  7. Update BUILD_STATUS.sxp
  8. PROCEED AUTOMATICALLY to next step (no user prompts)
  ↓
All steps complete
  ↓
BUILD COMPLETE"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Step 0: Configuration Collection")
      (para "**Purpose:** Collect ALL configuration decisions upfront")
      (para "**Logic:**")
      (code "IF BUILD_CONFIG.json exists at builds/BUILDNAME/BUILD_CONFIG.json THEN
  READ and display config
  SKIP to Step 1
ELSE
  SCAN steps/ for {{CONFIG:...}} markers
  FOR EACH marker:
    PROMPT user for value
    VALIDATE input
  END FOR
  WRITE BUILD_CONFIG.json with all values
  PROCEED to Step 1
END")
      (para "**Key Points:**")
      (item "Step 0 MUST run first - no exceptions")
      (item "If config exists, zero questions asked")
      (item "Enables fully autonomous Steps 1-N")
      (item "Machine-updatable for CI/CD variants"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Step N: Build Execution")
      (para "**Input:**")
      (item "Step file (ybs-step_<guid>.md)")
      (item "BUILD_CONFIG.json")
      (item "Previous step outputs")
      (para "**Process:**")
      (item "1. Read and parse step file")
      (item "2. Extract {{CONFIG:key}} placeholders")
      (item "3. Load BUILD_CONFIG.json")
      (item "4. Replace placeholders with config values")
      (item "5. Execute Instructions section")
      (item "6. Run Verification section")
      (item "7. Check results:")
      (item "All criteria met? → Success, proceed")
      (item "Criteria failed? → Retry (up to 3 attempts)")
      (item "3 failures? → STOP and report")
      (item "8. Record completion in build-history")
      (para "**Output:**")
      (item "Implemented code/features")
      (item "Test files")
      (item "Documentation")
      (item "Step-DONE file with timing")
      (item "Updated BUILD_STATUS.sxp")))
  (section
    (heading "Traceability System")
    (subsection
      (heading "In Source Files")
      (para "**Format:**")
      (code "// Implements: calculator-spec.md § 2.1 (Core Operations)
// Purpose: Provide basic arithmetic operations
import Foundation

func add(_ a: Double, _ b: Double) -> Double {
    return a + b
}")
      (para "**Requirements:**")
      (item "Every source file must reference its specification")
      (item "Format: `// Implements: <spec-file> § <section> (<feature-name>)`")
      (item "Optional: `// Purpose:` for additional context"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Verification")
      (para "**Command:**")
      (code "check-traceability.sh SYSTEM BUILD")
      (para "**Thresholds:**")
      (item "✅ PASS: ≥80% of source files have traceability comments")
      (item "⚠️ WARN: 60-79% traced")
      (item "✗ FAIL: <60% traced")
      (para "**Why It Matters:**")
      (item "Instant code review: Know WHY every line exists")
      (item "Specification updates propagate to code")
      (item "No orphaned code (code without purpose)")
      (item "AI can regenerate code from specs")))
  (section
    (heading "Tools and Utilities")
    (subsection
      (heading "check-traceability.sh")
      (para "**Purpose:** Verify code-to-spec references")
      (para "**Usage:**")
      (code "check-traceability.sh system-name build-name")
      (para "**Output:**")
      (item "Percentage of traced files")
      (item "List of untraced files")
      (item "Pass/Warn/Fail status"))
    (subsection
      (heading "list-specs.sh")
      (para "**Purpose:** List all specifications for a system")
      (para "**Usage:**")
      (code "list-specs.sh system-name")
      (para "**Output:**")
      (item "All spec files with size and title")
      (item "Organized by category"))
    (subsection
      (heading "list-steps.sh")
      (para "**Purpose:** Show build steps in execution order")
      (para "**Usage:**")
      (code "list-steps.sh system-name [--verbose]")
      (para "**Output:**")
      (item "Step number, GUID, title")
      (item "With --verbose: objectives and timing estimates"))
    (subsection
      (heading "deps.sh")
      (para "**Purpose:** Show feature dependency tree")
      (para "**Usage:**")
      (code "deps.sh system-name step-guid")
      (para "**Output:**")
      (item "Required specs")
      (item "Optional specs")
      (item "Conflicting specs")
      (item "Dependent features")))
  (section
    (heading "Complete Workflow Example")
    (subsection
      (heading "Building a Calculator System")
      (para "**System:** 02-calculator (reference example)")
      (para "**What it builds:** CLI calculator with add, subtract, multiply, divide operations")
      (para "**Structure:**")
      (code "02-calculator/
├── specs/
│   └── calculator-spec.md           # Complete specification
├── steps/
│   ├── STEPS_ORDER.txt
│   ├── calc-step_000000000000.md    # Step 0: Configuration
│   ├── calc-step_478a8c4b0cef.md    # Step 1: Project setup
│   ├── calc-step_c5404152680d.md    # Step 2: Calculator module
│   ├── calc-step_89b9e6233da5.md    # Step 3: Parser module
│   ├── calc-step_a1b2c3d4e5f6.md    # Step 4: Formatter
│   ├── calc-step_b2c3d4e5f6a1.md    # Step 5: CLI interface
│   ├── calc-step_c3d4e5f6a1b2.md    # Step 6: Unit tests (calc)
│   ├── calc-step_d4e5f6a1b2c3.md    # Step 7: Unit tests (parser)
│   ├── calc-step_e5f6a1b2c3d4.md    # Step 8: Integration tests
│   ├── calc-step_f6a1b2c3d4e5.md    # Step 9: Documentation
│   └── calc-step_a2b3c4d5e6f7.md    # Step 10: Final verification
└── builds/
    └── demo/                         # Example build")
      (para "**Execution Timeline:**")
      (item "**Total:** ~3 hours (175 minutes)")
      (item "Step 0: 5-10 minutes (configuration)")
      (item "Steps 1-5: 70 minutes (implementation)")
      (item "Steps 6-8: 55 minutes (testing)")
      (item "Steps 9-10: 35 minutes (documentation & verification)")
      (para "**Outcomes:**")
      (item "✅ Complete working calculator")
      (item "✅ Comprehensive unit tests")
      (item "✅ Integration tests")
      (item "✅ Full documentation")
      (item "✅ ≥80% code coverage")
      (item "✅ ≥80% traceability")
      (item "✅ All requirements verified")))
  (section
    (heading "YBS as Transport-Independent Framework")
    (subsection
      (heading "Critical Insight for YX Integration")
      (para "**YBS is COMPLETELY independent of how it's invoked or transported.**")
      (para "**YBS Defines:**")
      (item "✅ WHAT (specifications)")
      (item "✅ HOW (build steps)")
      (item "✅ WHY (traceability, decisions)")
      (para "**YBS Does NOT Define:**")
      (item "❌ Communication protocol")
      (item "❌ Message format")
      (item "❌ Network layer")
      (item "❌ Transport mechanism"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Implication")
      (para "YBS works with ANY transport:")
      (item "Direct file system access (current)")
      (item "HTTP/REST API calls")
      (item "**YX protocol (UDP/RPC)**")
      (item "SSH remote execution")
      (item "WebSocket streaming")
      (item "Message queues")
      (item "Any network protocol"))
    (subsection
      (heading "YX Implementation Strategy")
      (para "When implementing YBS on top of YX:")
      (item "1. **YBS layer stays exactly the same**")
      (item "Specifications remain unchanged")
      (item "Build steps remain unchanged")
      (item "Verification logic remains unchanged")
      (item "2. **YX layer is the transport**")
      (item "Messages flow over UDP")
      (item "RPC calls for requests/responses")
      (item "Packet security via HMAC/AES-GCM")
      (item "3. **Mapping layer connects them**")
      (item "Converts YBS requests to YX RPC calls")
      (item "Converts YX responses to YBS data structures")
      (item "Handles errors and retries")
      (para "**Example Flow:**")
      (code "AI Agent (YBS client)
  ↓ [Request: \"Read spec file calculator-spec.md\"]
YX RPC Call: ybs.readFile(path=\"specs/calculator-spec.md\")
  ↓ [YX UDP packet, HMAC, encryption]
YBS Server (file system access)
  ↓ [Read file, return content]
YX RPC Response: {content: \"...file contents...\"}
  ↓ [YX UDP packet, HMAC, encryption]
AI Agent receives content
  ↓ [Continue building]")))
  (section
    (heading "AI Agent Rules for YBS Execution")
    (subsection
      (heading "Core Rules")
      (item "1. **Execute Step 0 first** - Always, no exceptions")
      (item "2. **Check for BUILD_CONFIG.json** - If exists, skip questions")
      (item "3. **Read steps completely** - Understand full context before starting")
      (item "4. **Replace CONFIG values** - Substitute all placeholders with config values")
      (item "5. **Follow instructions exactly** - Don't improvise or skip steps")
      (item "6. **Verify before proceeding** - Don't skip verification checks")
      (item "7. **Retry failed steps** - Up to 3 attempts per step")
      (item "8. **Proceed autonomously** - No \"Ready for next step?\" prompts")
      (item "9. **Update status files** - Track progress in BUILD_STATUS.sxp and SESSION.md")
      (item "10. **Document timing** - Record actual elapsed time in step-DONE files"))
    (subsection
      (heading "What Success Looks Like")
      (para "**Completed Build:**")
      (item "All steps executed in order")
      (item "All verification criteria met")
      (item "All tests passing")
      (item "Code coverage ≥80%")
      (item "Traceability ≥80%")
      (item "BUILD_STATUS.sxp shows 100% complete")
      (item "No SESSION.md (deleted on completion)")
      (item "Complete system ready for use")))
  (section
    (heading "YBS Value Proposition")
    (subsection
      (heading "What YBS Enables")
      (para "✅ **Zero-interruption builds** - No questions after Step 0 ✅ **Full autonomy** - AI builds complete systems without human intervention ✅ **Complete traceability** - Every line of code traced to specification ✅ **Reproducible builds** - Same specs + same steps = same output ✅ **Language-agnostic** - Works for any programming language ✅ **Platform-agnostic** - Works for any operating system ✅ **Domain-agnostic** - Works for any type of software ✅ **Crash recovery** - Resume from interruption ✅ **Parallel execution** - Multiple agents building different systems ✅ **Machine-updatable config** - CI/CD variants with zero human interaction"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Core Value Statement")
      (para "> **Write specifications once. AI agents build complete systems from scratch, in any language, on any platform, infinitely, without human intervention, with full traceability and reproducibility.**")
      (para "This is fundamentally different from:")
      (item "Traditional development (code-first, specs-later, manual work)")
      (item "Manual AI prompting (fragmented, no traceability, constant interruptions)")
      (item "Other specification-driven tools (incomplete, require interaction, no autonomy)")
      (para "**YBS is the complete methodology for autonomous AI software development in 2026.**")))
  (section
    (heading "Summary")
    (para "YBS is a meta-framework that transforms software development from a manual, code-first process into an **autonomous, specification-driven process** where AI agents build complete systems from human-written specifications.")
    (para "**Key characteristics:**")
    (item "Configuration-first (Step 0 collects all decisions)")
    (item "Specification-driven (specs are source of truth)")
    (item "Verification-driven (explicit success criteria)")
    (item "Fully autonomous (zero interruptions after Step 0)")
    (item "Transport-independent (works with any communication layer)")
    (para "**Perfect for YX integration** because YBS defines the \"what\" and \"how\" of building, while YX provides the secure, efficient \"transport\" for distributed YBS operations.")))
